---
title: Dumpling 2-Minute Noodles
servings: 1
course: dinner
tags: quick, one-pan, noodle
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/M-PuGg7Ek-w/maxresdefault.jpg
source: https://youtu.be/M-PuGg7Ek-w
time: 5m
---

Bring @water{500%ml} to a boil in a #saucepan{}. Add @frozen dumpling{6} and cook for ~{2%minutes}, stirring occasionally so they do not stick to the bottom.

Open the @instant ramen{1%packet} and empty the seasoning sachets into the water, stirring to form the broth. Place the ramen noodles into the saucepan and let them begin to cook.

Slice @spring onion{2}, keeping the thicker sliced white parts and the finely sliced green parts separate.

Once the noodles begin to soften, stir them to break them apart. Add @peanut butter{1%tsp} and the white spring onion slices, stirring until dissolved into the broth. Simmer until the noodles are cooked and the dumplings are heated through, about ~{2%minutes}.

Using #tongs{}, transfer the noodles into a #bowl{}. Arrange the dumplings on top and pour the hot broth over everything. Garnish with the reserved spring onion greens and @chilli crisp{1%tbsp}.
